  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="2">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Romscot">Romscot</ref> 2</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="2" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="474" ed="#liebermann"/>Gif hit hwa forgumie, gylde LX scill' 7 be twelffealdan agife þene Rómpenincg.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="474" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn es jemand versäumt, zahle er 60 Schill. und entrichte den Rompfennig mit Zwölffachem.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If anyone neglects it, let him pay 60 shillings and render the Rome-penny twelvefold.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#unattributed" corresp="#wit-g-a">If anyone misses [this date], he should pay [a fine of] 60 shillings, and pay twelve times [the Peter's pence].</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="368"><label>term recurs</label> <ref target="clause:Northu_57-1">Northu 57.1</ref> <quote>the 'Rompenincg' of Romscot 2 recurs in Northu 57:1</quote></note>
        <note type="editorial">In G, Iudex follows in the same hand.</note>
      </div>
    </body>
